    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0447" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.15/1651.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Russell</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-26T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1915—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department trusts situation foreshadowed in your November 20, 5 p.m. will not
                    materialize. The resignation of President Jiménes would be a matter of regret
                    and concern. The Department will be glad if you will so inform him and assure
                    him of our support in any efforts that he may undertake with a view to secure
                    peace and prosperity in Santo Domingo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
